                            // ************           Instance vs Model Based Machine learning             ************

// Instance Based 

Here model checks the similarity score of its nearest negihbours to classify its position , therefore we need to maintained trained data so new point will use its nearest points in the trained data
to cassify itself ex: KNN ... etc

// model Based

Here model uses trained data to derive a equation and therefore divides according to equation and whenever a new point comes it uses equation and reaches its desired point based on equation and here
we need not maintain the trained data and we can throw it because new data always goes according to equation ex: linear regression ... etc





